                                    <watches>3</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14307649" author="rdblue" created="Thu, 5 Feb 2015 17:56:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Fixed in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-parquet-mr/pull/118&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;PR #118&lt;/a&gt;. The reason to remove it now is to avoid linker errors if thrift 0.9.1 or later is found in the classpath. Other than this problem, updating to 0.9.2 builds and passes tests.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14307743" author="julienledem" created="Thu, 5 Feb 2015 18:45:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The trouble is that data corruption issues in Thrift will produce hard-to-debug OOM errors.&lt;br/&gt;
Another option is to lookup whether the method exists through reflection in a static block and set a boolean IS_READ_LENGTH_SETABLE or something equivalent.&lt;br/&gt;
Then the block becomes:&lt;br/&gt;
```&lt;br/&gt;
if ( IS_READ_LENGTH_SETABLE) &lt;/p&gt;
{
      ((TBinaryProtocol)protocol).setReadLength(record.getLength());
 }
&lt;p&gt;```&lt;br/&gt;
and now we won&apos;t have linking issues.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14307775" author="rdblue" created="Thu, 5 Feb 2015 19:00:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;That works? I didn&apos;t think linking was done lazily like that. Either way, we can definitely do this through reflection if it&apos;s valuable.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14339338" author="rdblue" created="Thu, 26 Feb 2015 22:45:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I don&apos;t think the one-time reflection strategy works. I get compile errors when I build against 0.9.2. Is it safe to build against 0.9.0 or 0.7.0 and assume it works in 0.9.2?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;[ERROR] Failed to execute goal org.apache.maven.plugins:maven-compiler-plugin:3.1:compile (&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;-compile) on project parquet-thrift: Compilation failure
[ERROR] /home/blue/workspace/parquet-mr/parquet-thrift/src/main/java/parquet/hadoop/thrift/ThriftBytesWriteSupport.java:[136,34] cannot find symbol
[ERROR] symbol:   method setReadLength(&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;)
[ERROR] location: &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;class &lt;/span&gt;org.apache.thrift.protocol.TBinaryProtocol
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14339340" author="rdblue" created="Thu, 26 Feb 2015 22:46:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I could pretty easily add a version that uses a &lt;tt&gt;Method&lt;/tt&gt; field to do this with &lt;tt&gt;invoke&lt;/tt&gt;, but I don&apos;t know that it&apos;s a good idea. Is it possible to do this check in another way?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14348030" author="rdblue" created="Thu, 5 Mar 2015 02:46:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I updated the PR to use the one-time reflection strategy. I verified that it is binary compatible with 0.9.2, but cannot be built against 0.9.2.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;d like to find a better way to introduce this check, maybe one that works with all of the protocols by limiting the ByteBuffer (or whatever) passed to thrift?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14357720" author="rdblue" created="Wed, 11 Mar 2015 22:22:23 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Issue resolved by pull request 118&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-parquet-mr/pull/118&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-parquet-mr/pull/118&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17857143" author="rok" created="Sun, 23 Jun 2024 03:27:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This issue has been migrated to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-java/issues/1729&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;issue #1729&lt;/a&gt; on GitHub. Please see the &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-2502&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;migration documentation&lt;/a&gt; for further details.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
